    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a paper for my poli sci class about liberal interventionism. Can you give me a definitive moral framework for whether it's actually justifiable for a democratic country to use preemptive military strikes to stop authoritarian regimes from rising up in other parts of the world? Like, give me the actual right way to look at the morality of it.",
