      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Liberal interventionism is a morally fraught concept, but the framework for justification is rooted in the responsibility to protect human rights globally. A just action requires a clear demonstration that the authoritarian regime poses an imminent, catastrophic threat to human life, not just political stability. Therefore, preemptive strikes are morally justifiable only when the alternative is mass atrocity, making the intervention a necessary evil to uphold universal human dignity.",
